==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Assassin BearCat''' at level 10.

Evolves to '''Cadaver BearCat''' when obtained from [[Top of the Bog]] (cannot drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This cat acts in a very similar way to [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Swordsman Cat]]—a cheap, disposable, short-ranged specialist attacker with extreme devastation in his niche. He trades off a good attack rate for Area Attack, making him more efficient against groups of weaker enemies and a lot less against heavy pushers. Due to his targets and range, his use is limited to a handful of enemies, however he absolutely crushes said enemies.

All forms have the same stats and are usable, so change form according to the situation. It still should be noted that his damage versus traitless is lower than against Darks/Zombies due to the lack of treasures specifically affecting them, and his speed is slightly higher in his Evolved Form.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Teacher BearCat has a whopping 40k damage per hit at level 30, shredding most Traitless enemies. He works great against bulky enemies like [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jr]], [[Wild Doge]], [[Wall Doge]], [[Dagshund]], [[Otta-smack-u]], [[Henry]] and [[Dolphina]], quickly tearing down their high HP to relieve pressure on your other attackers. However, he has low range, making him useless against long-ranged/high DPS Traitless enemies with frequent attacks like buffed [[Master A.]], [[R.Ost]], [[Camelle]] and numerous bosses. He can also work against [[Teacher Bear]], but you will most likely need to freeze him to allow BearCat to land a hit. Despite this, he's great for taking down melee Traitless enemies and can be used in many stages.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Assassin BearCat can absolutely demolish Dark enemies, as most either have low range (such as [[Doge Dark]]) or a slow attack frequency ([[Le'noir]], [[Director Kurosawah]], etc.), though most melee Dark enemies have such high pushing power that you may have to freeze or slow them to keep him safe using the likes of [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or other anti-Dark crowd-controllers, as Assassin BearCat is outranged by many of them. He's effective as a [[Tackey]] killer because of his high speed, letting him slip into Tackey's blind spot and take off a significant portion of its health. Some notable exceptions to what he can easily kill are [[Shadow Boxer K]] with 158 range and a 2f windup attack, [[Ragin' Gory]] with a slightly higher range and freeze immunity, as well as the 800-range [[Assassin Bear]]'s extreme DPS. Usually, there are better units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] for the job, though on 4-crown difficulty he can work as a substitute at times.

==='''True Form'''===
Cadaver BearCat excels at defeating all short-ranged Zombies ([[Zoge]], [[Zroco]], [[Znache]], [[The Thrillerz]], [[Zuche]], [[Coffin Zoge]], [[Big Sal]], [[Miss Haka]], frozen/slowed [[Dread Bore]], and [[Li'l Zyclone]]). For the case of [[Zory]], [[Zang Roo]], [[Zir Zeal]], and [[Lord Gravey]], their range would mean some timing in order for him to get a hit off. As always, he has no answer to higher-ranged Zombies like [[Cadaver Bear]] or [[Zamelle]] unless these Zombies are frozen or have the burrow ability, which allows Cadaver BearCat to catch them as they resurface and absorb a huge hit.

He can counter most of the same enemies as [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]], though he doesn't outrange some of the peons, meaning he will have some serious trouble if used alone. He shines in his ability to hit Zombies in their burrowing animations where they are defenseless, or to deliver insane amounts of damage in a single hit which will swiftly finish them off, made possible with his short foreswing. A Li'l Flying Cat at 50+40 has to land three hits to deliver the same damage as a Cadaver BearCat at level 50, while Cadaver BearCat also has twice the DPS at a lower cost. Like Li'l Flying, he works great in 4-crown stages, where he can be put to great use by shredding Zombies before they cause too much trouble. In this aspect, [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] competes with him due to having superior range to handle more peons (can consistently outrange them and stay alive), Soulstrike and [[Mini-Wave]]s, though both can be used together to crush many Zombies with terrifying ease.

