==Trivia==
*The Japanese name of the play Teacher BearCat stars in, "Forest Teacher Bear" (もりのクマ先生 ''Mori no Kuma-sensei''), could be a throwback to the [[Nyanko Defence Force]] boss "Mr. Forest Bear" (森のクマさん ''Mori no Kuma-san'').
*"Bear of the Living Dead" is a reference to the famous zombie film ''[[wikipedia:Night of the Living Dead|Night of the Living Dead]]''.
**The Japanese name, "Forest Teacher Bear of THE END" (もりのクマ先生of THE END), could be a reference to the Japanese names of either ''[https://akurasu.net/wiki/Super_Robot_Wars/Masou_Kishin_F Super Robot Wars OG Saga: Masou Kishin F – Coffin of the End]'' or ''[[wikipedia:Yakuza: Dead Souls|Yakuza: Dead Souls]]'', being ''スーパーロボット大戦OGサーガ 魔装機神F COFFIN OF THE END'' or ''龍が如くOF THE END'' respectively.
*Assassin BearCat is significantly faster than his other two forms, in reference to [[Assassin Bear]]'s incredible speed compared to other teacher bear variants.
*For some reason, the "Insane" in Cadaver BearCat's description is capitalized when Teacher BearCat and Assasin BearCat's descriptions have the "insane" in lowercase.
*Teacher BearCat was the first non&ndash;Legend Rare unit to gain the insane damage ability.

